================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

LitUbik bundles or depends on the following. Each remains under its own licence;
this section records the ones that carry an obligation or that a redistributor
needs to know about. A machine-generated inventory of every transitive
dependency is in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md; the Windows release also ships
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt, the full licence texts of the bundled packages.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PyMuPDF / MuPDF — GNU AGPL v3, or a commercial licence from Artifex
    https://github.com/pymupdf/PyMuPDF
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Used for PDF text extraction, reference mining and bulk PDF import.

This is the reason LitUbik itself is AGPL and cannot be relicensed under
permissive terms: PyMuPDF is copyleft, and the AGPL forbids adding restrictions
downstream. Anyone wanting to ship a derivative under a non-AGPL licence must
obtain a commercial licence from Artifex, or replace this dependency.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PyInstaller — GPL v2 or later, WITH the bootloader exception
    https://pyinstaller.org
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Build-time only, used to produce the Windows executable. The exception
explicitly permits distributing the generated executable under any licence, so
the packaged build carries LitUbik's own terms and not PyInstaller's.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bibtexparser — LGPL v3 or BSD (dual)   |   certifi — MPL 2.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Both are file-level copyleft at most and impose no obligation on LitUbik beyond
preserving their own notices (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt in the Windows build).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
axe-core — MPL 2.0   |   lightningcss — MPL 2.0
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Development and build tools only (the accessibility audit run in CI, and the
CSS minifier used by the frontend build). Neither is shipped in the
application.

